<title>ITALY: Fiat, Rhone-Poulenc recycling deal.</title>
<headline>Fiat, Rhone-Poulenc recycling deal.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Fiat Auto said it has signed a deal with France's chemicals group Rhone-Poulenc for the recycling of used catalytic converters.</p>
<p>Fiat said in a statement that in the last year alone it had recycled over 1,500 catalytic converters and the total was set to double in 1997.</p>
<p>The use of catalytic converters only became obligatory in Italy in 1993.</p>
<p>Under the accord with Rhone-Poulenc, Fiat will salvage the platinum, rhodium and palladium metals from the converters as well as recycling the rest.</p>
<p>No financial details were given.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
